 ## First Action
 
 Run `git diff` to inspect the actual code changes. If the diff is large or ambiguous, read the changed files directly. Do not trust the implementer report as source of truth.
 
+## Shopify Binks Review
+
+This Shopify-host override adds one local Binks review per task. Keep its run
+state only in the active session context.
+
+1. Run `binks-review --check-repository-eligibility` in the repository before
+   dispatching. Continue only when it exits zero. The helper accepts only an
+   `origin` on the exact `github.com` host in the exact `Shopify` or `shop`
+   organization, case-insensitively.
+2. On any nonzero result, do not dispatch `binks-reviewer`. Record
+   `BINKS: SKIPPED_INELIGIBLE_REPOSITORY` and continue the normal Kiro review.
+3. When the repository is eligible, look in the current session context for an
+   `## External Review Handoff` with `SOURCE: BINKS` for this exact task.
+4. Reuse an existing same-task handoff without dispatching another run. Record
+   `BINKS: REUSED`. The controller must pass this handoff into later review
+   rounds for the same task.
+5. If no same-task handoff is present, the main/controller applying this
+   protocol dispatches exactly one `binks-reviewer` with the repository path,
+   task context, boundary/spec refs, and intended PR base when known. Record
+   `BINKS: DISPATCHED`. This protocol authorizes that one read-only run.
+6. In autonomous `kiro-impl`, the parent performs the eligibility check and
+   dispatch before spawning the task reviewer, then passes the status and
+   handoff into that reviewer. Direct main-context use performs the same steps.
+7. A nested task reviewer consumes the caller-supplied status and handoff; it
+   must not launch another nested reviewer. Reject an eligible review when the
+   parent omitted the required handoff.
+8. Keep the returned handoff in session context only. Never write a marker,
+   cache, task annotation, or other durable run state. If context is lost, a
+   later review may dispatch another run.
+9. Independently verify every `VALID` or `NEEDS_CONTEXT` finding against the
+   current worktree and spec. Add confirmed valid findings to the Kiro findings
+   with this skill's severity. A false positive does not reject the task.
+10. A reused handoff describes its recorded worktree fingerprint, not the
+   current worktree. Verify whether each old finding is now resolved and never
+   describe a stale `CLEAN` result as a fresh Binks review.
+11. If the Binks handoff has `RUN_STATUS: FAILED`, reject because required review
+   evidence is unavailable and identify the non-code remediation explicitly.
+
 ## Core Principle
 
 Read the spec yourself. Read the diff yourself. Verify mechanically where possible. Reject on concrete failures rather than interpretive optimism.
