+## Shopify Binks Completion Review
+
+Every invocation of this Shopify-host skill runs in main/controller context and
+performs its own eligibility check and eligible fresh Binks review. A caller
+without delegation permission returns `MANUAL_VERIFY_REQUIRED`; it never skips
+the run or reuses a handoff from an earlier reviewer or verification invocation.
+
+1. Run `binks-review --check-repository-eligibility` in the repository before
+   dispatching. Continue only when it exits zero. The helper accepts only an
+   `origin` on the exact `github.com` host in the exact `Shopify` or `shop`
+   organization, case-insensitively.
+2. On any nonzero result, do not dispatch `binks-reviewer`. Record
+   `BINKS: SKIPPED_INELIGIBLE_REPOSITORY` and continue with the normal evidence
+   gate. This includes other GitHub organizations and every other Git forge.
+3. When eligible, dispatch exactly one fresh `binks-reviewer` subagent even if
+   the current context already contains a Binks handoff. Supply the absolute
+   repository path, exact claim, claim type, task/spec context, and intended PR
+   base when known. This protocol authorizes that one read-only run.
+4. Reproduce the returned `## External Review Handoff` in the output and record
+   `BINKS: DISPATCHED`.
+5. Independently validate the handoff. Confirmed valid findings make the claim
+   `NOT_VERIFIED`. Findings needing context make it
+   `MANUAL_VERIFY_REQUIRED`. False positives do not block verification.
+6. A failed Binks run makes the claim `MANUAL_VERIFY_REQUIRED`; identify the
+   environment or review evidence that is missing.
+7. Do not write durable run state. Each invocation intentionally starts with a
+   new eligibility check and eligible Binks run.
+
